# Draft knowledge entry: open62541 static consumer validation on shadow CI

id: DRAFT-open62541-shadow-ci-static-library-1.5.6
trigger_tool: shadow-ci|conan|cmake|ld|llvm-readelf
phase: packaging|linking|testing|runtime
error_signature: static library package has no executable|cross-building.*runtime execution skipped|open62541 server created successfully
severity: 2
category: ci|conan|test-package|static-library|open62541
match_keywords: open62541, static library, test_package, UA_Server, shadow CI, L1, L2, L4, L5, destructive negative validation
title: validate an open62541 static package through a real consumer and classify executable smoke as skipped
root_cause: >
  A static library package has no package executable to run. An executable-only
  smoke rule can therefore report a false failure even when the installed
  library is consumable. The meaningful runtime object is the consumer program.
affected_scope: >
  Static C/C++ Conan packages whose public API can be exercised by a small
  deterministic consumer without an external service.
verification_cmd: >
  conan test archives/o/open62541/1.5.6/test_package
  open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64;
  require consumer compile/link and device execution; classify package
  executable smoke as L2 skip when no bin/ exists.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: consumer-first-static-package-test
rec_description: >
  Build a C consumer that creates and minimally configures UA_Server, links it
  to open62541::open62541, and runs it on the OHOS shadow device. During
  cross-build, compile/link only. Retain a destructive negative check that
  removes the library payload from an isolated copy and proves the consumer
  cannot pass accidentally through a system prefix.
rec_command: >
  conan create archives/o/open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: static-library-consumer-validation
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: enable-upstream-test-dependency
fallback_description: >
  If broader coverage is required, run open62541's Check-based unit tests as a
  separate test-only task. Do not turn Check into a production dependency just
  to manufacture a package executable.
fallback_command: conan install --requires=check/0.15.2 --build=missing
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: separate-test-dependency
forbid_1_pattern: mark missing package bin/ as a package build failure
forbid_1_reason: Static library packages are expected to have lib/ without bin/.
forbid_1_consequence: Valid library packages are incorrectly rejected by smoke gates.
forbid_2_pattern: claim Windows cross-build as runtime-tested
forbid_2_reason: AArch64 OHOS ELF execution belongs on an OHOS device or target runner.
forbid_2_consequence: Runtime evidence is false and can hide device-only failures.
principles: consumer-centric-testing, static-package-classification, destructive-negative-test
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
